card.statement:
Let $r\ge2$ and $m\ge2$.

[(i)]

- The polynomials $P_{-2r,n}(c)$ satisfy the fourth-order linear ordinary differential equation

\begin{equation}
(c^2-1)^2 m^2 r^4\,P_n^{(\mathrm{iv})}
+10c(c^2-1)m^2 r^4\,P_n'''
+\bigl[X^{(1)}_n c^2+Y^{(1)}_n\bigr]P_n''
+Z^{(1)}_n\,c\,P_n'
+W^{(1)}_n\,P_n = 0,
\end{equation}

where

\begin{align}
W^{(1)}_n &= n(n-2r)\bigl(m(n-2r+2)+2r\bigr)\bigl(m(n-4r+2)+2r\bigr),  \\[3pt]
X^{(1)}_n &= r^2\bigl(-2m^2((n+2)n+2)+4mr(m(2n+3)-n-2)+r^2(3m(5m+4)-4)\bigr),  \\[3pt]
Y^{(1)}_n &= r^2\bigl(2m^2((n+2)n+2)-4mr(m(2n+3)-n-2)-16mr^2\bigr),  \\[3pt]
Z^{(1)}_n &= -3r^2\bigl(m^2(-8nr+2(n+2)n+5r^2-12r+4)+4mr(n-3r+2)+4r^2\bigr).
\end{align}

- The polynomials $P_{-r,n}(c)$ satisfy the fourth-order linear ordinary differential equation

\begin{equation}
(c^2-1)^2 m^2 r^4\,P_n^{(\mathrm{iv})}
+10c(c^2-1)m^2 r^4\,P_n'''
+\bigl[X^{(2)}_n c^2+Y^{(2)}_n\bigr]P_n''
+Z^{(2)}_n\,c\,P_n'
+W^{(2)}_n\,P_n = 0,
\end{equation}

where, setting $\Delta = r^2(r-2)m(2mn-7mr+2m+4r)$,

\begin{align}
W^{(2)}_n &= (n^2-r^2)\bigl(m(n-5r+2)+2r\bigr)\bigl(m(n-3r+2)+2r\bigr), \\[3pt]
X^{(2)}_n &= -2r^2\!\left(m^2\bigl((n-r)(n-2r)-10r^2\bigr)+2mr(n-3r)+2r^2\right)+\Delta, \\[3pt]
Y^{(2)}_n &= \phantom{-}2r^2\!\left(m^2\bigl((n-r)(n-2r)-(2r^2+r)\bigr)+2mr(n-4r)\right)\nonumber\\
&\quad-r^2(r-2)m\bigl(2mn-6mr+2m+4r\bigr), \\[3pt]
Z^{(2)}_n &= -3r^2\!\left(2m^2(n-r)(n-2r)+4mr(n-3r)+4r^2\right)+3\Delta.
\end{align}
